# Tracer: not-equality symmetry is a builtin rule with checked Lean evidence.
#
# Before (Litex verified, but To-Lean rejected the proof route):
# forall a set, b set:
#     $is_set(a)
#     $is_set(b)
#     a != b
#     =>:
#         b != a
# Former behavior: Litex cited `a != b` as if it were already the differently
# oriented goal `b != a`; To-Lean rejected that changed citation because it had
# no structured symmetry evidence.
#
# Now (verified and compiled from builtin proof evidence):
forall a set, b set:
    $is_set(a)
    $is_set(b)
    a != b
    =>:
        b != a
# Current behavior: the verifier records not-equality symmetry with the checked
# premise `a != b`; To-Lean emits one shared `{α}` carrier and `Ne.symm` for
# `b != a`.
#
# Boundary: without either orientation of a non-equality fact, the rule remains
# unknown; the executable negative boundary lives in not_equal_builtin.rs.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/01_proof_patterns/not_equal_symmetry.lit
# Compiler evidence: cargo test --release not_equal_symmetry -- --nocapture
# Lean kernel evidence: LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=<mathlib-project> LITEX_LAKE=<lake-path> cargo test --release generated_not_equal_symmetry_compiles_with_lean -- --ignored --nocapture
# Implementation: src/to_lean/type_context.rs, src/to_lean/set_prelude.rs,
# src/to_lean/to_lean_pipeline.rs, and src/verify/verify_builtin_rules/not_equal_builtin.rs
